comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T16:07:50.190Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full live open/in-progress lists and specific budget/Sentry searches plus complete all-status corpus contain no exact active owner. Full live pm-ju83 metadata/history confirms the broad graph platform is completed; the open recovery-closure feature is the parent. New report PM-CLI-3N contains4 handled CLI events with exit1 on the published release, separate from this branch's publisher work. Evidence is sanitized to exclude host paths identities and payloads. The literal budget-floor producer and existing regression are located before implementation."
  "2026-10-19T16:15:08.946Z","harness:codex","The repaired negative control is semantic: two regressions fail and25 existing tests pass. Direct SDK command callers receive a raw TypeError instead of an expected usage error, and MCP lets the same budget-floor exception escape. The initial malformed test edit is not counted as defect evidence. The command-layer fix converts only the existing controlled budget-floor signal, uses public expected-error and command-rendering helpers, preserves cause and compact executable recovery, and leaves low-level kernel TypeErrors and unrelated fatal errors unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T16:16:00.751Z","harness:codex","SDK and real CLI recovery acceptance now pass. The MCP test initially invoked the internal dispatcher, which deliberately propagates errors to the transport; corrected the test to drive the actual JSON-RPC line processor and inspect its emitted tool-error envelope. No MCP production behavior is changed. The original command-layer negative control remains valid; the earlier direct-dispatch MCP expectation is not claimed as transport evidence."
  "2026-10-19T16:20:50.099Z","harness:codex","Linked sandbox acceptance passes all51 tests:22 dependency-command cases,24 low-level relationship/history cases and5 MCP cases. The real CLI returns usage2 and structured invalid_argument_value, the suggested compact retry executes successfully, the JSON-RPC tool envelope retains recovery, and the primitive retains TypeError. All4 TypeScript projects and SDK surface check pass with0 classified export changes. Original published Sentry events remain preserved and unresolved until delivery acceptance; the next-release boundary must remain explicit."
  "2026-10-19T16:23:00.616Z","harness:codex",Static contract validation detected the new producer location for the existing invalid_argument_value code. Ran the maintained error-code generator; its only catalog change adds sdk/dependencies.ts to that existing code. No code shape or public export changes. The failed stale-catalog gate is retained and the complete static gate is rerun after regeneration.
  "2026-10-19T16:37:58.638Z","harness:codex","Fresh GH1513 reports the same infeasible-budget defect plus a related hard-ceiling failure. Independently reproduced in a separate CLI-initialized temporary tracker with telemetry disabled: legacy related_to counts and max-depth0 yield JSON budget300 success with400 emitted estimated tokens and495 reported; budget800 reports495 for400 emitted. TOON300 emits286 tokens. Extend this active leaf to settle final alias/projection/lean bytes and refuse an impossible rendered floor rather than returning oversized success. Four separate new context/cursor reports remain open and unclaimed under their own intake leaves."
  "2026-10-19T16:53:32.211Z","harness:codex","Rendered-byte negative controls fail3 cases and pass21 existing cases before the hard-ceiling correction. Final linked acceptance passes99 tests. A dependency-command-only diagnostic has exact100/100/100/100 coverage:328 statements228 branches61 functions311 lines. Its scope is diagnostic; unchanged repository-wide100% remains a hosted requirement. Final bytes include populated legacy aliases, omitted row-discovery suppression, optional discovery, lean JSON, JSON output-format selection, configured encoding and token accounting. Host invocation metadata preserves the original caller aliases; default collapse none must not fabricate a migration hint. Initial and rendered-floor refusals return usage2 with executable compact inspection, while malformed cursors still propagate their original error. Lower-level TypeError validation is unchanged. The linked command was replaced through remove/add because command identities are immutable; original failed and successful run evidence remains in history."
  "2026-10-19T16:57:08.937Z","harness:codex","Final-source acceptance is exercising fresh get/list/contracts plus an intentional expected budget refusal and this evidence mutation. Verify exact telemetry pairs, usage2/invalid_argument_value failure classification, recent handler spans, empty physical queue and preserved historical Sentry events before release-aware closure. Per-process sampling only; no persistent configuration change."
  "2026-10-19T17:43:57.635Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit source review adds two accepted requirements: report the requested and a verified feasible context-retry budget, with exact minimum only when bounded exhaustive verification establishes it; cap missing-reference retries by actual rows. A separate isolated archived-source control fails1 case with28 passes because the compact recovery loses the selected tracker in a foreign workspace. The scope-preserving retry now passes99 linked tests. Preserve the original report scope and public low-level exceptions; numeric advice must be verified rather than guessed, and expensive searches must disclose limits."
  "2026-10-19T18:01:37.973Z","harness:codex","Review remediation: preserve the tracker and original context selection/output policy in a verified numeric retry; keep tree-summary inspection separate. A bounded real-packer search reports requested tokens, verified feasible tokens, and an exact minimum only after exhaustive lower-budget proof. Larger or independently constrained queries explicitly disclose an unproved/unavailable minimum. The empty-reference loop now starts at the actual row count. Three accepted head-f67 review findings remain pending committed verification; no scope split because this delivery follows the requested related BIG PR."
  "2026-10-19T18:05:12.693Z","harness:codex","Local recovery acceptance now passes 225 cases across five focused files, including real canonical context retries under all JSON policies, an exact minimum with a failing immediately-smaller budget, output-constraint unavailability, MCP metadata, foreign-workspace routing and bounded empty-reference retries. Four TypeScript projects and strict repository ESLint pass. The generated SDK surface flags optional interface additions as signature changes; the maintained updater records the explicit non-breaking optional-field rationale, with compile-time producer/consumer checks."
  "2026-10-19T18:07:40.388Z","harness:codex","The aligned final tests reject archived f67 source in both controls: numeric recovery metadata is absent, and empty-reference builds grow from 1008 to 3008 as edgeLimit grows from 1000 to 3000. Corrected source passes all 228 cases in six focused files. Scoped V8 coverage for deps, budget search and public error helpers is exact 100/100/100/100: 453 statements, 336 branches, 80 functions, 425 lines. This scoped diagnostic is not substituted for the required whole-project gate. Contract/catalog checks, docstrings and duplicate lint pass."
  "2026-10-19T18:27:07.545Z","harness:codex","Exact-head a235 review inventory is CLEAN with no unresolved inline threads, but a new top-level actionable report identifies an encoding-precedence gap: explicit json:false with configured default JSON is measured as JSON even though formatOutput selects TOON. It belongs to this same rendered-byte owner. Reproduce across context/tree/graph before changing the shared selection condition; retain expected-refusal and retry-policy controls. CodSpeed also reports a small fingerprint regression with cross-runtime and uninstrumented-syscall qualifications; assess that separately under the existing performance owner."
  "2026-10-19T18:32:32.306Z","harness:codex","Explicit TOON/default-JSON precedence is reproduced at a235 in all three dependency formats: context reports414 versusactual278, tree262 versus182, graph277 versus179 tokens in the synthetic controls. One shared condition now matches the final renderer and preserves TOON in numeric retries. 296 linked tests pass; scoped recovery/error coverage remains exact100/100/100/100 across453 statements337 branches80 functions425 lines. Head-a235 required PR checks are green/CLEAN, but its full Native run39300409994 has separate macOS1/Windows2 failures under investigation; neither is labeled accepted."
  "2026-10-19T18:32:48.765Z","harness:codex","Evidence correction for the preceding synthetic TOON control: the captured context comparison is396 reported versus277 actual tokens, not414 versus278. Tree262/182 and graph277/179 were transcribed correctly. The raw failing-before receipt remains /tmp/pm-toon-override-negative-control.log; subsequent acceptance uses measured equality rather than hardcoded token totals."
  "2026-10-19T18:39:45.232Z","harness:codex","Sentry resolution is now tied to fixing commit22edcd089d4dff47baf04a839ec75be7ac2813f8, with no inRelease binding. The attempted @next operation returned current release2026.10.19, so it was immediately undone and replaced with the verified commit binding. Published v2026.10.19 is not claimed fixed. Four original issue events remain preserved; expected refusal telemetry and the successful foreign-workspace retry provide fresh production-stack evidence."
  "2026-10-19T18:41:10.307Z","harness:codex","Required Sentry/telemetry gate now passes with the issue resolved in fixing commit22ed (not published v2026.10.19). The current-source probe records paired starts/finishes for get,list,contracts and expected deps usage2; the real foreign-workspace retry succeeds at exactly756 emitted tokens. Fresh Sentry spans include these successful reads, telemetry flush and the successful deps retry. Expected refusals add no issue event. Head-a235 whole-project coverage is exact100/100/100/100; final source22ed awaits its own checks and complete platform acceptance."
  "2026-10-19T18:59:40.340Z","harness:codex","Full head22ed review audit includes resolved-thread revisions and the updated walkthrough: CodeRabbit completed with no actionable inline findings and minimal merge risk. Its docstring advisory is also addressed with meaningful comments on the five changed undocumented functions; runtime behavior is unchanged. Its scope-splitting advisory is declined because this delivery follows the explicitly requested related BIG PR with seven linked implementation owners. Source22ed Native runtime cohorts all pass; only the now-corrected PM graph relation failed static quality."
  "2026-10-19T19:02:06.969Z","harness:codex","Final runtime acceptance at22ed is complete: all seven Native runtime jobs pass, including both Windows/macOS shards and Linux22/24/25. Ubuntu24 passes10811 tests with3 intentional skips and exact global100/100/100/100, zero uncovered counts.296 linked regressions and exact recovery/error scoped coverage also pass. CodeRabbit full review covers22ed with no actionable comments and minimal merge risk; existing findings are resolved. Later source edits add only the requested five private-function docstrings: comment-free transpilation of all three source files is identical. The sole hosted static failure was a true missing PM related edge; local graph-composition now passes at the unchanged1233 ceiling. Final reviewed-closeout head must still pass its own required checks. Sentry/telemetry gate passes0 critical/high with fix bound to22ed, preserving the current published-release boundary."
